{
    // Zero-Coupon ERG Bond, with pluggable liquidation, paying the holder of its bond asset
    // Holds the borrower's collateral until the loan is repaid in nanoERG before maturity,
    // or liquidated under the liquidation script both sides agreed to. Either way the lender's side goes
    // to the BondAssetVault, tagged with the bond asset, and whoever holds that asset claims it.
    //
    // REGISTERS
    // R4: Coll[Byte] - bondAssetId: the bond asset that claims this bond's payout. It is the box id of the
    //                  order or offer that created this bond, since that box was INPUTS(0) and minted it.
    // R5: Coll[Byte] - borrowerHash: blake2b256 of the borrower's ErgoTree bytes
    // R6: Coll[Long] - amounts: Idx 0 is the repayment in nanoERG, Idx 1 is the batching fee in nanoERG,
    //                  the most an executor may keep for itself when it liquidates this bond
    // R7: Int        - Bond Maturity Height. Repayment is open strictly below it.
    // R8: Coll[Byte] - liqScriptHash: blake2b256 of the serialized liquidation EXPRESSION, i.e. the exact
    //                  bytes executeFromVar runs. Not an ErgoTree, so not a propositionBytes hash.
    //                  UIs may filter bonds by known liquidation hashes.
    //
    // CONSTANTS
    // CONST_VAULT_HASH: Coll[Byte] - blake2b256 of BondAssetVault, where every settlement goes
    //
    // TOKENS
    // Only the collateral. The bond asset is never held here: the lender has the one unit there is.
    //
    // CONTEXT VARS
    // CTX_LIQ_SCRIPT(0): Coll[Byte] - the liquidation expression. Its presence selects the liquidation
    //                    path, so a repayment must leave it unset.
    //
    // OUTPUTS (index-paired: the bond at INPUTS(i) settles into OUTPUTS(i))
    // Liquidate: OUTPUTS(i)   collateral to the vault
    // Repay:     OUTPUTS(i)   repayment to the vault
    //            OUTPUTS(i+1) collateral back to the borrower
    // Both settlement boxes carry R4 = SELF.id, so one output can never settle two bonds. The vault's also
    // carries R5 = bondAssetId, the asset that claims it. Batching repayments still needs a "filler" input
    // between bond inputs, since each repayment takes two outputs.
    //
    // ASSUMPTIONS
    // - The order or offer that created this box pinned every register, minted exactly one unit of the
    //   asset R4 names, and bounded the batching fee to 0 <= fee <= SELF.value - min box value. None of that
    //   is re-checked: a bond built by hand can name any asset in R4, and only pays that asset's holder.
    // - R8 is trusted completely, including WHEN liquidation is allowed: this contract never compares
    //   HEIGHT to maturity on the liquidation path. The order must only accept liquidation scripts the
    //   borrower agreed to; a script that is always true lets the bond be liquidated at once.
    // - Repayment is permissionless: anyone may pay the lender in full and return the collateral.
    // - The batching fee is a ceiling, not a payment. Nothing says where the difference goes, so the
    //   transaction builder keeps it. A lender liquidating their own bond may simply take everything.

    val bondAssetId      = SELF.R4[Coll[Byte]].get
    val borrowerHash     = SELF.R5[Coll[Byte]].get
    val amounts          = SELF.R6[Coll[Long]].get
    val repayment        = amounts(0)
    val batchingFee      = amounts(1)
    val maturityHeight   = SELF.R7[Int].get
    val liqScriptHash    = SELF.R8[Coll[Byte]].get
    val collateralAssets = SELF.tokens
    val collateralERG    = SELF.value

    // Shared by both paths, so evaluating these eagerly costs neither path anything it does not need
    val settlementBox    = OUTPUTS(CONTEXT.selfBoxIndex)
    val toVault          = blake2b256(settlementBox.propositionBytes) == CONST_VAULT_HASH
    // R5 is what the vault opens with. Unpinned, a settler could name an asset of its own there and
    // claim the lender's box from the vault itself.
    val settlementTagged =
        settlementBox.R4[Coll[Byte]].get == SELF.id &&
        settlementBox.R5[Coll[Byte]].get == bondAssetId

    val liquidationScript = getVar[Coll[Byte]](0)

    if (liquidationScript.isDefined) {
        val liquidated = allOf(
            Coll(
                blake2b256(liquidationScript.get) == liqScriptHash,
                toVault,
                settlementTagged,
                settlementBox.tokens == collateralAssets,
                settlementBox.value  >= collateralERG - batchingFee
            )
        )
        sigmaProp(liquidated) && executeFromVar[SigmaProp](0)
    } else {
        // Collateral box returned to borrower. Read only here, so a liquidation of the last bond in a
        // transaction does not need an output after it.
        val returnBox = OUTPUTS(CONTEXT.selfBoxIndex + 1)
        val repaid = allOf(
            Coll(
                HEIGHT < maturityHeight,
                // RepaymentBox Conditions
                toVault,
                settlementTagged,
                settlementBox.value >= repayment,
                // ReturnBox Conditions
                blake2b256(returnBox.propositionBytes) == borrowerHash,
                returnBox.R4[Coll[Byte]].get == SELF.id,
                returnBox.tokens == collateralAssets,
                returnBox.value  >= collateralERG
            )
        )
        sigmaProp(repaid)
    }
}
